LICENSE OVERVIEW

Keybow Firmware Plus is a fork of Pimoroni's Keybow firmware:
https://github.com/pimoroni/keybow-firmware

This repository contains components under different licenses. No single license covers every file.

Original Keybow C firmware, Lua scripts, and example patterns:
MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Pimoroni Ltd. The original MIT license is reproduced below.

Keybow Firmware Plus editor code and project-created assets:
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 ThoughtfulDev. See editor/LICENSE.

bcm2835 1.68:
GPL-3.0-only. Full text in bcm2835-1.68/COPYING.

libusbgx:
The library is LGPL-2.1-or-later. Example sources are GPL-2.0-or-later. See libusbgx/COPYING.LGPL and libusbgx/COPYING.

Lua 5.4.0:
MIT. Copyright and license text are in lua-5.4.0/doc/readme.html.

Raspberry Pi boot firmware:
Redistribution terms are in sdcard/LICENCE.broadcom.

Linux kernel and initrd packages:
The kernel is GPL-2.0. Initrd packages retain their individual notices under /usr/share/doc/*/copyright. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for firmware provenance and source-availability status.

Desktop application dependencies:
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for license information and required notices. Desktop package builds include that file.

The keybow executable statically links bundled components, including bcm2835 and libusbgx. Distribution of the combined executable is subject to the applicable copyleft terms and source-code obligations in those component licenses. The original Keybow MIT license does not apply to the combined executable or the entire repository.


